tten and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking Someone to Slow Down", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you ask someone to speak slowly, it is important to be polite.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Here are some phrases you can use to ask someone to speak slowing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Slow down, please! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Speak slowly please, Miss/Sir. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Again, slower please, Miss/Sir. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Would you mind speaking slower? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You are speaking very fast. Could you slow down, please?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense to talk about actions in the future.<br/><br/> The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is <span class=\"strong\">'ll</span>.<br/><br/>You use the Future tense when you talk about intentions, make offers or make predictions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Starting Monday, I'll do educational outreach at the company. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I'll write blogs and articles for the website.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Peace Corps", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an American organization that promotes international development", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you joining the Peace Corps? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le01ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear to talk about promotions at work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "How cool is that?", "type": "name"}, {"content"